e SDGs for quite a while but we  decided that we wanted to pay a little  bit more attention to blue tech blue  economy oceans and the sustainable  development goals related to that and so  there's a couple quick ways that if we  want to find out who is influential in  this area we can do it we can simply ask  Twitter  give me a Twitter ID search for blue  tech and then we can say give me the top  results from that and so we have one  input we can do in a form we can make it  fancy we can also say let's look at the  last 500 tweets about blue tech and I  want to know from those users that  tweeted about blue tech which of those  actually has the biggest influence and  we can follow  those but the problem with both of these  approaches is you have a relatively  relatively narrow scope of information  that you're bringing in you're only  looking at relevance instead of overall  influence or you're only looking at one  segment in time so what we've done we  started looking at is instead saying if  we want to understand who the  influencers are in an area it's actually  more important that we look at the  broader scope of what's going on in  Twitter and if any of you have spent the  time going through the Twitter API going  through the the service connect you'll  realize that Twitter builds in a lot of  limitations you can only get up to 500  tweets you can only request 15 friend  lists often it's time bound and so you  can only get the last 7 days or the last  30 days and so we wanted to start  combining different functions and  combining different queries so that we  could extrapolate even more information  and the idea for us is we believe that  if we know who a few influencers are we  know that as busy was saying in the SDG  world that you and Gaara  Euan goals is is a great one or I ISD is  another great one we can look at who are  they following because of an influencer  is following another influencer you can  bet that you've got some overlap and  then we can look at data related to  hashtags to see are we talking about the  same thing so in our case what we did is  we started with our own account and we  said let's take a look at who we're  following let's take a look at and who  is influential influential in this space  and let's start doing some analysis on  that  among those accounts we can then  download all of their hashtags and we  can say ok show me who my friends are  tweeting to show me what my friends are  talking about and we can see that a  picture starts to emerge about what  hashtags are actually most engaging or  most used in the space and so we say hey  we've got these 14 users that when we go  through our resources we know they talk  about what we're interested in and we  know that that they have enough  followers that there's somebody that we  should pay attention to  and so we download all the details about  these known  influences and you can see it ranges  from a thousand to a hundred thousand  but that doesn't matter because we know  that these people are tweeting on topic  if if you want to learn about impact  investing another area that we work you  can do the same thing there and figure  out who is talking about impact  investing and who are they following so  again with our known followers we can  pull their hashtags and say now what are  they talking about and this is a place  we can kind of check our math and see  like yeah we're talking about the same  thing so this is what we what we want to  see but the big jump where we start  going beyond what the Twitter API  provides and start providing our own  analysis is we do pull in the follower  list for each of those users so if I am  let's say that I am Scripps Institute  which is a great blue tech ocean related  organization if I'm in that space and  that's all I'm talking about if I look  at who I'm friends with who I think is  worth following we can start to build  that list and so what we've done is of  those 14 followers that we started with  